{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773939374,"nonce":"pZZouWrZ5Tq+wSjNQEeeqzymyKs=","title":"SDK Console UI: sidebar controls, remove Chat toggle, show user messages","message":"Three UI issues in the Console tab for SDK sessions:\n\n1. **SessionControls should be a collapsible right sidebar**, not below the input bar. Same vertical extent as the stream+input region (below the tab bar). Modern, attractive design.\n\n2. **Remove the \"Chat\" view-toggle button** for SDK sessions that have no debug terminal. The ViewToggle renders a lone \"Chat\" button that does nothing when `showDebugTerminal=false`. Hide the entire ViewToggle when there is only one mode.\n\n3. **User messages not shown in Chat view for SDK sessions.** The SDK event stream contains 0 `user` type events — the initial prompt is not echoed back by the SDK. Need to synthesize a user event in the stream when the prompt is submitted (similar to `synthetic_prompt` which already exists in StreamRenderer types). Also ensure consistency between Chat view and History view for both SDK and PTY sessions.\n\nNote: the user also observed that Allowed Tools in SessionControls does not interact with the Permissions dropdown (allow_always). This is a separate concern but worth noting.","files":null}]}